for _t in ["Effects are mean differences in days (DC or SL minus FC) for continuous outcomes and risk ratios for binary outcomes. Negative differences favour the experimental strategy. All bodies of evidence started at high certainty within the ROBINS-I framework.",
 "1. Risk of bias: downgraded one level. The overall ROBINS-I judgement was serious in 31 of 32 non-randomized studies, driven by confounding by indication, and the three randomized trials had some concerns (small, unblinded, one stopped early).",
 "2. Inconsistency: downgraded one level for I² of 50% to 74% and two levels for I² of 75% or more.",
 "3. Imprecision: downgraded one level when the 95% CI crossed the null or a minimally important difference (3 days for stay, feeds and parenteral nutrition, 1 day for ventilation, RR 0.75 to 1.25 for binary outcomes) and two levels when it also rested on fewer than five studies or fewer than 400 participants.",
 "Publication bias was not rated down (Egger P = 0.58 for stay, DC vs FC; fewer than 10 studies for other comparisons)."]:
    para(_t,size=8,after=2)
